hat you cannot know *which* traces, if any, this man carries—unless you look at him directly. The fair thing to do is to test for the traits you're worried about through behavioral questions, the same way you would for any candidate. If your intuition turns out to be right, you'll have real evidence. If it's wrong, you'll have avoided a serious mistake. Either way, you've treated him as a person, not a prediction.
